# Arc's AppleScript dictionary (Arc 1.172.1's Arc.sdef, same codes in resources/Cra.sdef): a window's
# active tab is readable, `execute javascript` is refused until View ▸ Developer ▸ Allow JavaScript from
# Apple Events is on (off by default, as in Arc), then runs in the tab. Scripts use raw codes, run inside Cra.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=scripted
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?applescript=tell%20current%20application%20to%20get%20%C2%ABclass%20URL%20%C2%BB%20of%20%C2%ABclass%20acTa%C2%BB%20of%20%C2%ABclass%20WiND%C2%BB%201
expect-log Cra applescript → http://127\.0\.0\.1:[0-9]+/page\.html\?n=scripted
cra://debug?applescript=tell%20current%20application%20to%20count%20%C2%ABclass%20tAbB%C2%BB%20of%20%C2%ABclass%20WiND%C2%BB%201
expect-log Cra applescript → .*1
cra://debug?applescript=tell%20current%20application%20to%20%C2%ABevent%20CrSuExJa%C2%BB%20%C2%ABclass%20acTa%C2%BB%20of%20%C2%ABclass%20WiND%C2%BB%201%20given%20%C2%ABclass%20JvSc%C2%BB%3A%226%2A7%22
expect-log Cra applescript → error .*Allow JavaScript from Apple Events
cra://action/allowAppleEventsJavaScript
cra://debug?applescript=tell%20current%20application%20to%20%C2%ABevent%20CrSuExJa%C2%BB%20%C2%ABclass%20acTa%C2%BB%20of%20%C2%ABclass%20WiND%C2%BB%201%20given%20%C2%ABclass%20JvSc%C2%BB%3A%226%2A7%22
expect-log Cra applescript → 42
